      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] The commit message narrates the exact code changes (\"assigning the .mux pointers and setting .next to NULL individually on each port\"). Commit messages should describe the conceptual change rather than transcribing the diff.\n\nConsider this more concise, non-narrating replacement:\n\n```text\nampton: Fix usb_mux override corruption and alignment check crash\n\nIn board_customize_usbc_mux(), ampton copied ampton_usb_muxes (an array\nof struct usb_mux) into usb_muxes using memcpy(usb_muxes,\nampton_usb_muxes, sizeof(ampton_usb_muxes)).\n\nWhen usb_muxes was updated across octopus to use struct usb_mux_chain,\nthis memcpy remained, overflowing the smaller usb_mux_chain array and\ncorrupting the chain pointers with raw struct usb_mux bytes on any board\nwith board_version \u003e 0. During early init, configure_mux() traversed the\ncorrupted chain, dereferenced an invalid mux pointer, and triggered a\nGeneral exception [Alignment check] crash loop at ~15 ms after boot.\n\nFix this by properly initializing the `usb_mux_chain` structures for each\nport instead of using a bulk memory copy.\n\nBUG\u003dNone\nTEST\u003dmake BOARD\u003dampton\nTEST\u003d/mnt/336bcd7c-aca6-4625-b004-42e4e240ad3d/chromiumos/chromite/bin/cros format --check board/ampton/board.c\nTEST\u003d/mnt/336bcd7c-aca6-4625-b004-42e4e240ad3d/chromiumos/chromite/bin/cros lint board/ampton/board.c\n\nChange-Id: I8a69ad846cdfaa51bde525587e67247010f3f50a\n```\n[🔗](http://go/tj/b800808f-d694-426a-89fe-2534b313a1b4)",
